WHY GPL-2.0
------------

BootPatcher ships and modifies Linux kernel images. The Linux kernel is
GPL-2.0, and the output of this tool is a modified kernel image, so the
source here is distributed under the same terms.

You must include a copy of the GPL-2.0 when redistributing patched boot
images, and offer the corresponding source of the kernel you used.


VENDORED THIRD-PARTY CODE
-------------------------

app/src/main/assets/magiskboot
    Extracted unmodified from the official Magisk APK release
    (topjohnwu/Magisk, https://github.com/topjohnwu/Magisk), specifically
    lib/arm64-v8a/libmagiskboot.so.

    Magisk is GPL-3.0. Copyright (C) 2018-2025 Topjohnwu.
    Source: https://github.com/topjohnwu/Magisk

    This is the ARM64 build, so the patching engine runs on the phone. The
    x86-64 build in bin/magiskboot is used instead by the GitHub Actions
    runner and remains under the same license.

bin/magiskboot
    x86-64 build of magiskboot used by the Telegram bot workflow on the
    GitHub Actions runner. Same origin and license as the asset above.


BUNDLED KERNELS
---------------

No kernels are vendored. BootPatcher downloads artifacts from
nothingnesscore/BruhKernel at runtime. Those images are covered by the
BruhKernel GPL-2.0-only license and its NOTICE.


